diagnosis_text:
Thorough end-to-end testing of every path mentioned in the ticket reveals no network fault. PC3 (10.3.0.100/24, default gateway 10.3.0.1) is fully connected and reachable from every direction tested. Direct gateway reachability (10.3.0.1 on dswb1.br0.10) succeeds in under 1 ms. Inter-office paths to pc1 and pc2 in Office A succeed with 0% packet loss at ~2 ms RTT. Intra-Office-B connectivity to srv1 (VLAN 30, 10.5.0.4) succeeds via the routed inter-VLAN path. The WAN router r1 is also reachable. The VLAN data plane is correctly configured throughout: aswb2.eth0 carries PC3 as PVID=10 Egress-Untagged; the trunk ports (eth1 to dswb1, eth2 to dswb2) carry all four VLANs; both distribution switches present the correct Layer 3 SVI gateways for each VLAN. The early observation of TX=0 bytes on PC3 was a transient idle condition (the container had received multicast/broadcast frames but had not yet transmitted any unicast traffic); it resolved immediately once traffic was generated. Whatever maintenance activity occurred overnight either caused a fault that has since self-healed, or the user's perception of loss was not caused by the network configuration. The correct action is to close the ticket as no-fault-found and advise the user to retest — if symptoms recur, capture them in real time for investigation.
=== END ===